The main change is to resolve the active subfield index once into a local, so the function has a single call to `SetFLOAT64Value` instead of two. Call order and conditions match the original, so behavior is unchanged. The gain is small, since the function is a thin wrapper.

```cpp
void Mesg::SetFieldFLOAT64Value(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum, const FIT_FLOAT64 value, const FIT_UINT8 fieldArrayIndex, const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex)
{
    if (!CanSupportSubField(fieldNum, subFieldIndex))
        return;

    Field *field = AddField(fieldNum);

    if (field == FIT_NULL)
        return;

    FIT_UINT16 resolvedSubFieldIndex = subFieldIndex;
    if (subFieldIndex == FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_ACTIVE_SUBFIELD)
        resolvedSubFieldIndex = GetActiveSubFieldIndex(fieldNum);

    field->SetFLOAT64Value(value, fieldArrayIndex, resolvedSubFieldIndex);
}
```